Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(models): drive backend concurrency limits from the catalog

The llama-cpp backend hardcoded limits.maxConcurrentBatches: 1. The indexing policy
clamps with Math.min(requestedConcurrency, maxConcurrentBatches), so every value was
clamped to one worker -- including an explicit --index-embedding-concurrency and
ZVEC_GREP_INDEX_EMBEDDING_CONCURRENCY. The automatic path collapsed to one worker
too, because neither llama-cpp nor transformers-js mapped the catalog's
defaultConcurrency into the model info; only model2vec did.

Map defaultConcurrency into the model info for both backends and use it for
maxConcurrentBatches, so the catalog entry is the single source of truth for local
embedding concurrency. The default stays at one when a catalog entry does not
declare it.

 src/engine/models/backends/llama-cpp.ts      | 4 ++--
 src/engine/models/backends/transformers-js.ts | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/engine/models/backends/llama-cpp.ts b/src/engine/models/backends/llama-cpp.ts
index e78b08e..2b5138f 100644
--- a/src/engine/models/backends/llama-cpp.ts
+++ b/src/engine/models/backends/llama-cpp.ts
@@ -185,6 +185,7 @@ export class LlamaCppEmbeddingModel extends BaseEmbeddingModel {
       name: entry.model,
       dimension: entry.dimension,
       metric: entry.metric,
+      defaultConcurrency: entry.defaultConcurrency,
       inputKinds: ["text"],
       limits: {
         maxBatchSize: entry.maxBatchSize,
